    <h2>My journey</h2>
    <p>After facing cancer and becoming an empty nester, I found myself at a crossroads. Europe became more than a duty station. It became a canvas for healing, creativity and growth.</p>
    <p>SHE FLUTTER was born from that transformation: a space to style my life with purpose, document my book journey, and connect with other women navigating change.</p>

    <h2>Why SEASONS</h2>
    <p>SEASONS is a novel inspired by my life. It follows Imani, a girl who grew up in the furnace, as she learns to stop bracing, to be loved without being hurt, and to raise children who never have to hold their breath.</p>
    <p>It is a story about breaking a generational curse, and about the everyday work it takes to build a love that lasts.</p>
    <blockquote class="pull">Can a girl raised in the furnace learn to be loved, and to love, without burning anybody?</blockquote>

    <h2>Why SHE FLUTTER?</h2>
    <p>The name honors the flutter of uncertainty that comes with change, and the strength it takes to rise anyway. It’s about movement, grace, and the quiet power of reinvention.</p>

